Answers ranged from “0” to over “151 billion,” again revealing data quality issues. In addition, many participants provided the exact correct answer (40,320). When flagging outliers (> 99,616; Tukey, 1977) and correct answers, implausible responses were significantly more common in the Blocked Group (28%) than the Approved Group [11.4%, χ2(1, N = 567) = 25.12, p < .001, = – .210], and in the Open Sample (22.0%) compared to the Approved Group, [χ2(1, N = 586) = 11.87, p < .001, \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
